    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The edge-blind effect and utility trench vibrations seem like plausible culprits. However, I'm trying to understand if there's any scenario where the damage appears almost \"targeted\" or irregular, even though it follows a longitudinal path. We've even checked for localized moisture pockets and found nothing unusual. Is there any other mechanism where the pavement might just degrade from within or experience unexpected, localized \"attacks\" on its structural integrity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
